WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.790
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:10.060 --> 00:12.030
[Where are you? I'll come get you]

3
00:37.180 --> 00:38.690
Morning.

4
00:39.870 --> 00:41.540
Morning.

5
00:44.770 --> 00:47.080
Want me to come get you after work?

6
00:47.080 --> 00:49.100
No, it's fine.

7
00:49.100 --> 00:51.140
I'll be heading straight home today.

8
00:51.880 --> 00:55.000
Then can we eat dinner together?

9
00:56.010 --> 00:57.380
Sure.

10
00:57.380 --> 00:58.950
Great.

11
01:28.130 --> 01:31.220
- Your key? - Yeah... Oh.

12
01:31.220 --> 01:32.860
Thanks.

13
01:34.910 --> 01:36.350
Huh?

14
01:37.790 --> 01:40.460
Oh, sorry.

15
01:40.460 --> 01:43.600
It's fine. Thanks.

16
01:44.540 --> 01:47.050
See you later.

17
01:53.670 --> 01:55.240
Eita?

18
01:56.360 --> 01:59.400
Could you take time off work today?

19
02:00.490 --> 02:02.230
Is everything okay?

20
02:07.750 --> 02:10.780
Sorry. It's nothing.

21
02:12.670 --> 02:14.190
Take care.

22
02:38.400 --> 02:41.200
[4 years ago - Japan]

23
04:11.410 --> 04:13.440
Hello, it's your neighbor.

24
04:15.830 --> 04:18.170
I promise I'm no one suspicious.

25
04:39.090 --> 04:42.550
I'll be next door.

26
04:47.480 --> 04:51.790
I can't do much, but I am a neighbor.

27
04:54.520 --> 04:58.670
I'll leave the door open when I'm home.

28
05:01.220 --> 05:03.080
That's all.

29
05:04.350 --> 05:05.720
Good night.

30
06:15.410 --> 06:17.690
Mr. Nishikido?

31
06:17.690 --> 06:19.340
Ms. Tan Lei.

32
06:19.960 --> 06:21.710
We met at Xiufang's shop.

33
06:21.710 --> 06:24.920
Yes. I'm Sakura's partner.

34
06:25.650 --> 06:27.660
I manage the artworks left here.

35
06:27.660 --> 06:28.810
Would you like to see inside?

36
06:28.810 --> 06:31.520
No. Just the outside today.

37
06:33.300 --> 06:35.180
I see.

38
06:35.180 --> 06:38.680
Has there been any trouble selling this building?

39
06:41.770 --> 06:44.200
Would you feel better if it were gone?

40
06:47.270 --> 06:49.580
Sometimes, I think so too.

41
06:53.110 --> 06:55.540
I don't need to see inside.

42
07:00.800 --> 07:03.240
You want to go on without seeing it?

43
07:50.830 --> 07:52.830
What is this?

44
07:55.080 --> 07:58.410
He's drawn this many times since the accident.

45
07:59.130 --> 08:01.680
Did he remember this room?

46
08:03.440 --> 08:04.900
No.

47
08:06.830 --> 08:09.700
He thought it was a place he had never seen.

48
08:12.740 --> 08:15.410
He kept drawing the same woman.

49
08:16.960 --> 08:19.610
Without knowing who she was.

50
08:21.670 --> 08:25.410
When did he realize it was Sakura?

51
08:28.620 --> 08:30.930
After he met her again.

52
08:33.910 --> 08:36.230
Even though he forgot...

53
08:37.800 --> 08:42.680
He never stopped drawing.

54
08:44.430 --> 08:47.770
That's why you don't want them to see each other.

55
08:47.770 --> 08:50.800
Why did she come back here again?

56
08:50.800 --> 08:53.750
She doesn't remember anything.

57
08:53.750 --> 08:55.650
Wait.

58
08:55.650 --> 08:59.370
She doesn't remember?

59
08:59.370 --> 09:04.460
Her memories of the time she spent with Lun faded little by little.

60
09:06.910 --> 09:09.840
She's not pretending to have forgotten.

61
09:16.890 --> 09:20.250
But even without remembering,

62
09:23.840 --> 09:27.020
they both came back to the same place.

63
09:40.320 --> 09:44.810
I've watched Sakura for the last four years.

64
09:44.810 --> 09:47.010
And I've watched Lun.

65
09:48.100 --> 09:50.070
Then you understand.

66
09:50.070 --> 09:52.210
I don't know what's right.

67
10:02.460 --> 10:04.060
Excuse me.

68
10:34.610 --> 10:37.400
Your face looks terrible.

69
10:38.070 --> 10:39.350
Yeah?

70
10:39.350 --> 10:41.370
You look like you haven't slept.

71
10:45.910 --> 10:49.340
So? Did something happen?

72
10:53.860 --> 10:56.160
I saw them.

73
10:56.160 --> 10:57.800
Saw who?

74
11:00.880 --> 11:02.470
Your girlfriend?

75
11:05.050 --> 11:06.950
Ask her about it.

76
11:06.950 --> 11:08.300
I can't.

77
11:08.300 --> 11:10.180
Why not?

78
11:11.700 --> 11:14.700
Because asking might end everything.

79
11:19.170 --> 11:22.810
At least she still comes home.

80
11:25.810 --> 11:29.010
I envy Sakura.

81
11:29.650 --> 11:31.340
What?

82
11:31.340 --> 11:35.710
She's lucky to have someone who's so scared of losing her.

83
11:38.760 --> 11:43.610
Maybe she's "coming home", only because she has to.

84
12:09.720 --> 12:11.250
Come on in.

85
12:27.220 --> 12:29.650
You can leave the door open.

86
12:30.980 --> 12:32.060
What?

87
12:32.060 --> 12:34.560
I'm a stranger, and a man.

88
12:34.560 --> 12:37.110
You should be able to leave if you ever feel uncomfortable.

89
12:39.300 --> 12:42.810
Not that I plan on doing anything, of course.

90
12:46.570 --> 12:48.710
Are you hungry?

91
12:50.850 --> 12:52.780
A bit.

92
12:52.780 --> 12:55.810
Then come eat.

93
13:38.780 --> 13:42.700
I'm so sorry. I can't believe I fell asleep.

94
13:44.220 --> 13:45.920
It's fine.

95
13:46.470 --> 13:48.360
Feel free to sleep all you want.

96
13:55.090 --> 13:59.830
You're always welcome to relax at my place.

97
13:59.830 --> 14:03.140
You can leave at any time as well.

98
14:03.980 --> 14:05.420
See?

99
14:06.190 --> 14:08.630
The door is still open for you.

100
14:11.760 --> 14:13.330
Please...

101
14:15.240 --> 14:18.220
Don't feel obligated to help.

102
14:18.220 --> 14:20.130
Obligated?

103
14:20.130 --> 14:26.020
You have no reason to help me.

104
14:27.460 --> 14:31.000
Do I need a reason to lend a hand?

105
14:31.670 --> 14:37.070
You'll only exhaust yourself, and fast.

106
14:39.380 --> 14:42.110
Helping others...

107
14:43.490 --> 14:45.580
It's tiring.

108
14:48.520 --> 14:52.000
Then I'll tell you if I ever tire out.

109
14:54.310 --> 14:59.010
I want to see you fully recover, Ms. Sakura.

110
15:00.100 --> 15:03.820
I didn't want to tie her down.

111
15:04.830 --> 15:09.540
I just wanted to become a place she could call home.

112
15:10.690 --> 15:13.860
[How about nikujaga for dinner?]

113
15:29.780 --> 15:32.360
You still have to make some.

114
15:32.360 --> 15:34.950
There's already a lot, though.

115
15:50.760 --> 16:03.700
[White pepper]

116
16:03.700 --> 16:07.670
[Lun's Secret Recipe] [White pepper is key]

117
16:15.950 --> 16:18.620
- I'm home. - Welcome back.

118
16:21.090 --> 16:22.520
You're cooking today?

119
16:22.520 --> 16:24.210
Yeah.

120
16:24.210 --> 16:28.010
White pepper? That's an unusual pick.

121
16:28.010 --> 16:29.150
Really?

122
16:29.150 --> 16:32.540
Yeah. I don't see you use it often.

123
16:36.540 --> 16:38.800
How about I cook for us instead?

124
16:38.800 --> 16:40.230
No, I want to...

125
16:40.230 --> 16:42.300
I can't have you overexerting yourself.

126
16:42.300 --> 16:43.980
Just leave it to me.

127
16:59.060 --> 17:00.820
Are you tired?

128
17:02.950 --> 17:04.620
No.

129
17:09.490 --> 17:11.680
Tell me if anything's wrong, okay?

130
17:12.360 --> 17:14.510
I'll be here to listen.

131
17:17.250 --> 17:18.670
Okay.

132
17:28.620 --> 17:30.210
Sakura.

133
17:39.400 --> 17:41.000
Sorry.

134
17:43.300 --> 17:46.520
No, it's just... I'm tired.

135
17:46.520 --> 17:50.040
Yeah. I know.

136
18:02.870 --> 18:05.080
I want us to go back to normal, and yet...

137
18:26.820 --> 18:28.740
What are you drawing?

138
18:34.190 --> 18:35.870
I don't know.

139
18:38.390 --> 18:40.260
You met her again?

140
18:52.730 --> 18:54.400
Did I...

141
18:56.590 --> 18:58.830
Did I love her?

142
19:07.750 --> 19:10.210
Don't you already know the answer?

143
19:14.770 --> 19:16.620
Erase that sketch.

144
19:29.930 --> 19:32.100
This is my hand.

145
19:34.960 --> 19:37.470
Did I hurt her?

146
19:40.400 --> 19:43.350
Why can't I remember anything?

147
19:44.830 --> 19:46.620
Why?

148
20:06.750 --> 20:09.160
[Keep this, until I want to remember]

149
20:13.280 --> 20:14.930
[Lun]

150
20:14.930 --> 20:16.210
"Lun".

151
20:21.950 --> 20:23.930
"203".

152
20:25.490 --> 20:27.180
[Accident - Rain] [Ambulance - Red Lights]

153
20:27.180 --> 20:30.190
"An accident". "Rain".

154
20:31.820 --> 20:33.990
[Day 3: I still remember his voice]

155
20:33.990 --> 20:36.440
"I still remember his voice".

156
20:37.510 --> 20:39.780
[Day 10: His voice sounds far] [Trying to remember hurts my head]

157
20:39.780 --> 20:41.940
"His voice sounds far".

158
20:42.970 --> 20:45.330
[One month: His face is a blur] [Yet my chest hurts]

159
20:45.330 --> 20:47.620
"His face is a blur".

160
20:48.270 --> 20:51.270
[Three months: I can't remember his name] [without writing it out]

161
20:51.270 --> 20:53.340
"I can't remember".

162
20:53.340 --> 20:55.930
[6 months: Who is it I've forgotten?] [Did I really want to forget?]

163
20:55.930 --> 20:59.030
"Who is it I've forgotten?"

164
20:59.570 --> 21:02.240
[It's not that I've forgotten] [Every day, he gets further away]

165
21:02.240 --> 21:04.750
"It's not that I've forgotten".

166
21:04.750 --> 21:08.520
"Every day, he gets further away".

167
21:11.670 --> 21:14.110
"Eita. I entrust this truth to you."

168
21:14.110 --> 21:17.070
"The truth, of the day I broke."

169
21:18.810 --> 21:26.220
[But the key to 203] [is the one thing I can't give you]

170
21:27.300 --> 21:32.680
She couldn't entrust me with 203.

171
22:02.620 --> 22:05.140
You can leave the door open.

172
22:06.540 --> 22:07.550
What?

173
22:07.550 --> 22:09.920
You should be able to leave if you ever feel uncomfortable.

174
22:41.840 --> 22:44.050
I'll leave the door open.

175
22:51.280 --> 22:59.050
[Next]
